verity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the literal-IP / private-address rejection reuses the existing `ipaddress`-based classification (see _mcp_auth.py's `is_loopback/is_private/is_link_local` guard), factoring a shared helper if so, rather than re-deriving the private-range rule in terraform_source.py.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:276 and :432 already classify IP literals via `ipaddress.ip_address(host)` with `ip.is_loopback or ip.is_private or ip.is_link_local` at construction time (DNS not resolved)","That code is inlined per auth-endpoint-class, not exposed as a shared helper; the plan's surface (globally-routable DNS target, cross-host redirect, per-host credential trust) is materially broader, so it is not a clean rebuild — but the IP-literal/private classification specifically is the same primitive"],"finding":"The network-target validation's literal-IP / private-address rejection overlaps an existing inlined SSRF classifier in _mcp_auth.py; the plan does not name whether it reuses that ipaddress-based check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0461bf5ad42b10f1","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Registry metadata (\"Reject ... literal IPs ... a private-address custom host requires the exact credentialed hostname\")","norm_id":"n140cc1ccc4777d23","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer probes a custom registry host given as a literal IP or a private-range address","A future change to the private-range definition drifts between _mcp_auth.py and terraform_source.py"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"