ts it will call Terraform Registry 'service discovery and version/metadata endpoints' but never names the concrete endpoint paths, so the specific external surfaces cannot be verified as MATCH against Terraform's documented Registry protocol (they are UNVERIFIED). Endpoint granularity is the T3 unit: an unnamed new endpoint surface is an asserted-but-unverified external capability the plan depends on.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff43bca558bb7b23a","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Registry metadata","norm_id":"n2047a9bfde37463f","priority":0.11,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The discovery document path or the provider-versions vs module-versions path is mis-specified at implementation time, so a valid public/registry source is probed at the wrong path and abstains (or the download-URL negative oracle is written against a wrong endpoint shape).","A reviewer/verifier cannot confirm the probe restricts itself to metadata-only endpoints without the concrete paths named."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the classification for a same-host / otherwise-unenumerated non-2xx (esp. 3xx under the no-redirect opener) response so every HTTP status maps to either a 2xx-schema-valid positive or a closed abstention reason_detail (e.g. treat any non-2xx that is not an already-mapped code as `network_error`).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3112,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'Redirect-following is DISABLED (no-redirect opener): a cross-host redirect is `network_error`'","Plan: 'A 2xx schema-valid response yields only count/digest/source-kind facts'","Access-matrix AC enumerates '401/403/404, 429, DNS, TLS, proxy, 5xx, rejected redirect, timeout, malformed JSON, and oversized response' — no generic/same-host 3xx bucket","deps.py `_probe_registry` classifies only 200/404/410/429/5xx/transport; a no-redirect opener returning a 3xx status is a new case this backend did not face"],"finding":"Under the DISABLED-redirect (no-redirect opener) mechanism, a non-2xx response that is NOT one of the enumerated matrix codes — specifically a same-host 3xx redirect status, or any other unlisted 3xx — has no specified classification. The success branch is 'a 2xx schema-valid response'; cross-host redirect maps to rejected_redirect/network_error; but a same-host 3xx (which a no-redirect opener surfaces as a raw 3xx status rather than following it) falls through both the success path and the enumerated abstention matrix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c94b60fba9af0ee","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope → Registry metadata (redirect handling) and Acceptance Criteria → access-matrix AC","norm_id":"nec3b777a5ecc499d","priority":0.2888,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A registry host answers the discovery or version endpoint with a same-host 301/302/307 (e.g. trailing-slash canonica